WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.860
Pickups have a long tradition of a simple
concept: driver up front, cargo in the back.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:24.360
Today we'll look at the newest developments
in pickups, starting with the Fiat Fullback.Based

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:30.420
on the Mitsubishi L 200, it relies on proven
Japanese high-volume-production technology.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.120
It comes with either rear-wheel or all-wheel
drive.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:41.230
Under the hood is the newest generation of
Mitsubishi's light-alloy, 4-cylinder, 2.4-liter,

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.780
133-kilowatt engine.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:48.790
We tested it with the 5-speed automatic transmission,
but it comes alternatively with a 6-speed

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.340
manual transmission.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.469
A ladder frame with coil springs in front
and leaf springs in back means the Fullback's

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:01.789
ride is not that comfortable.

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:04.470
But off-road, it tackles just about anything.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.750
The all-wheel drive, gear reduction, and a
lockable center differential make you feel

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.480
you could go anywhere.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.060
Tester Christof says the Fullback would
be perfect for fetching wood for his fireplace

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.070
twice a year.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.420
But it's just too big for the rest of the
time.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.580
Nissan's Navara, with all-wheel drive and
a double cab, costs more than 31,000 euros

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.310
in Germany.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.900
And if you equip it as lavishly as our test
car, you quickly get closer to 40,000 euros.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.119
What clearly sets the Navara apart from its
competitors: the double-cab version we're

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:54.180
driving, with two rows of seats, is the only
one with coil springs rather than leaf springs.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.640
That makes it more comfortable to drive than
the competitors, while it's just as competent off-road.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.120
Despite being outfitted with stabilizers,
the axles work together perfectly.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.620
Rear-wheel drive is the Navara's default.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.560
But when needed, you can manually switch to
four-wheel drive.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.080
And the central differential can be locked.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.960
Like the Fiat Fullback, the Navara has a classic
steel frame ensuring that the car doesn't

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:29.360
fall apart even with the roughest treatment,
for example, when towing heavy trailers.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.340
The Navara is the only pickup certified to
tow 3.5 tons.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.600
Spending two years in Australia gave car tester
Moritz an affinity for vehicles like the Nissan Navara.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.240
But while it's prepared for anything in the
Outback, it's not ideal for the big city.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:55.700
The current Toyota Hilux is already the eighth
generation of this legend among off-road pickups.

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:59.450
For more than 50 years, its been the world's
universal transport.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.390
18 million Hiluxes have been built.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.300
It's hard to be a bigger legend.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.800
And it wouldn't be easy to make the Hilux
any more robust.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:17.010
But Toyota says the new model's steel-frame
body makes it even more solid.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.230
That's hard to imagine when you know that
millions of Hiluxes have been put to the toughest

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.490
tests and still hold up after decades.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.020
You'd think there would be nothing left to
improve.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.580
And subjectively, it's not easy to tell.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:39.069
The Hilux is like a fortress.

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:43.180
The engine pulls and the wheels rumble as
they always have.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:49.280
The price for the Hilux with all-wheel drive
and a double cabin begins at almost 35,000 euros.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.820
But if you want one as nice as our test car,
you'll be pushing 40,000 euros here, too.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.680
Jochen Frerichs says the Hilux has been
THE construction-site vehicle all over the

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:06.010
world for almost 50 years.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.780
It's robust through and through.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.340
Jochen's only criticism?

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.860
The 150-horsepower engine is a bit weak and
not certified to pull more than 3.2 tons.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.060
Otherwise, this is the most iconic pickup
of all.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.840
There's a difference between the three pickups.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.620
All of them climb steep grades effortlessly.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.760
But downhill is a different matter.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.560
Only the Toyota and the Nissan have electronic
hill descent control to help them move down

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.200
gravel roads safely.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:42.740
They all have in common the little-boy thrill
you get when taking the driver's seat.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:48.530
All three feel like they were made for playing
in that great big sandbox, the world.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.380
The open beds offer some practical advantages.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.030
But hardly anyone would use them regularly,
except on the job at construction sites and

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.509
the like.

00:04:57.509 --> 00:05:01.420
These trucks are big, cumbersome fuel-guzzlers.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:10.620
In sum: We see the disadvantages but love
these vehicles anyway for being so different.

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:15.120
And after a hard day's work, what could beat
a few beers at a tailgate party?

